 ## Shared principles
-Builds on [Neural Radiance Fields](4972-neural-radiance-fields.md). All methods in this family rely on the differentiability of the forward rendering operator and the propagation of gradients through the integration steps. The core mechanism is the evaluation of the volume rendering equation and the computation of gradients with respect to scene parameters (density, geometry, transfer functions, camera poses).
+Builds on [Dynamic and Deformation Modeling](13664-dynamic-and-deformation-modeling.md).
 
 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Spline-based Deformation Field](11457-spline-based-deformation-field.md)
-This method parametrizes the deformation field in dynamic volume rendering using cubic B-splines with time-modulated weights to map spatial coordinates $(x, y, z)$ at time $t$ to canonical coordinates $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ [11457-spline-based-deformation-field.md]. It enables the reconstruction of dynamic scenes from sparse projection data by combining a pre-trained canonical volume with the learned deformation field [11457-spline-based-deformation-field.md]. Unlike Neural Deformation Fields which rely on MLPs and complex regularization, this approach allows reconstruction from as few as two projections due to the efficient encoding provided by B-splines [11457-spline-based-deformation-field.md].
+This method parametrizes the deformation field in dynamic volume rendering using cubic B-splines with time-modulated weights to map spatial coordinates $(x, y, z)$ at time $t$ to canonical coordinates $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ [Spline-based Deformation Field](11457-spline-based-deformation-field.md). It enables the reconstruction of dynamic scenes from sparse projection data by combining a pre-trained canonical volume with the learned deformation field [Spline-based Deformation Field](11457-spline-based-deformation-field.md). Unlike Neural Deformation Fields which rely on MLPs and complex regularization, this approach allows reconstruction from as few as two projections due to the efficient encoding provided by B-splines [Spline-based Deformation Field](11457-spline-based-deformation-field.md).
 
 ### [Deformation-Guided Neural Fields](12044-deformation-guided-neural-fields.md)
-Deformation-Guided Neural Fields address the problem of modeling dynamic, articulated subjects (specifically human faces) in neural radiance fields by decoupling identity from pose and expression [12044-deformation-guided-neural-fields.md]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods by explicitly guiding the deformation field MLP with a parametric 3D morphable model (3DMM), ensuring that the learned deformations adhere to anatomical priors rather than relying solely on unconstrained neural predictions [12044-deformation-guided-neural-fields.md].
