 ### [Neural Deformation Field](12724-neural-deformation-field.md)
-The Neural Deformation Field (NDF) is a method for modeling non-rigid, time-varying deformations in neural radiance fields by predicting per-point displacements in a canonical space [12724-neural-deformation-field.md]. It solves the problem of animating static neural representations without relying on rigid body assumptions or human-specific priors like SMPL [12724-neural-deformation-field.md]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like Deformation-Guided Neural Fields by explicitly decoupling the rigid skeletal transformation (LBS) from the residual non-rigid displacement predicted by a neural network [12724-neural-deformation-field.md].
+The Neural Deformation Field (NDF) is a method for modeling non-rigid, time-varying deformations in neural radiance fields by predicting per-point displacements in a canonical space [Neural Deformation Field](12724-neural-deformation-field.md). It solves the problem of animating static neural representations without relying on rigid body assumptions or human-specific priors like SMPL [Neural Deformation Field](12724-neural-deformation-field.md). It sets itself apart from sibling methods like Deformation-Guided Neural Fields by explicitly decoupling the rigid skeletal transformation (LBS) from the residual non-rigid displacement predicted by a neural network [Neural Deformation Field](12724-neural-deformation-field.md).
 
 ### [Local Rotation Estimation via SVD](14864-local-rotation-estimation-via-svd.md)
-Local Rotation Estimation via SVD is a technique used in dynamic neural radiance fields to correct view-dependent rendering artifacts caused by large rigid-body rotations during deformation [14864-local-rotation-estimation-via-svd.md]. It estimates the local rotation for each point in a deformed point cloud using Singular Value Decomposition (SVD), inspired by As-Rigid-As-Possible (ARAP) mesh deformation [14864-local-rotation-estimation-via-svd.md]. This estimated rotation is then interpolated to query view directions to "bend" rays, ensuring consistency between the deformed space and the canonical space representation [14864-local-rotation-estimation-via-svd.md]. It differs from sibling methods like [Neural Deformation Field](12724-neural-deformation-field.md) by explicitly modeling rotational components of the deformation field rather than relying solely on translation or dense deformation vectors, thereby handling complex fine-level deformations without introducing extra complexity into the radiance field model itself [14864-local-rotation-estimation-via-svd.md].
